# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# WHY: the 2026-07-31 build uploaded a 164 MB archive and EAS itself said so
# ("You can reduce its size ... by excluding files that are unnecessary").
# 78 MB of that was App Store LISTING material — store-screenshots/ (58 MB) and
# store-screenshots-clean/ (20 MB) — which the build never reads. It is
# compressed, uploaded, and thrown away on every single build, on every app.
#
# THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY COMPLETE, NOT A ONE-LINER. eas-cli consults
# .easignore, and the documented behaviour is that it takes PRECEDENCE over
# .gitignore rather than adding to it. If that is right, an .easignore listing
# only the screenshots would start shipping node_modules/, ios/, android/ and
# .env to EAS — far worse than the problem it set out to fix, and a secret leak
# besides. So this file restates every rule that matters from the root
# .gitignore and apps/customer/.gitignore. That makes it correct whether
# .easignore replaces .gitignore or merely supplements it.
#
# If you add an ignore rule to a .gitignore that affects this app, add it here
# too. A rule that exists in only one of the two is the failure mode this
# comment exists to prevent.

# ---- Dependencies and VCS -------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.git/

# ---- Generated / local build output ---------------------------------------
.expo/
.export/
dist/
web-build/
ios/
android/
expo-env.d.ts
*.log
*.orig.*

# ---- Secrets. Never upload these. -----------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
credentials/
*.p8
*service-account*.json

# ---- Local binaries -------------------------------------------------------
*.ipa
*.aab
*.apk

# ---- Store listing material: needed by humans, never by a build -----------
# This is the 78 MB. Keep it in the repo; just stop shipping it to EAS.
store-screenshots/
store-screenshots-clean/
store-assets/

# ---- Repo docs ------------------------------------------------------------
*.md

.DS_Store
